  "notes": [
    "Pads: 8x8 grid sends Note On/Off ch 1, bottom-left = 36 .. top-right = 99 \u2014 the keyboard block renders exactly that range; velocity = pressure.",
    "All 10 encoders + jog are RELATIVE (CW=1, CCW=127, accelerate on fast turns): the console shows raw deltas, not positions. Buttons are momentary (press=127, release=0).",
    "Touch sensors (Notes 0-13: encoders 0-7, volume 8, tempo 10, jog 11, strip 12, D-pad 13) are notes, not CCs \u2014 not bindable as controls (wire law).",
    "Touch strip position is pitch bend on ch 1 \u2014 not CC-bindable.",
    "Push 2 differences (same layout, mostly identical): New = CC 87 (not 92), Master/Stop Clip = CC 52/53, Browse = CC 111, Swing encoder = CC 15 (which Push 3 uses for the tempo-encoder press).",
    "Sending absolute CCs back to encoder CC numbers for LED feedback is unverified on real hardware \u2014 treat writes to encoders as experimental.",
    "Aftertouch: poly pressure per the map; tethered Push 3 with MPE showed channel pressure instead \u2014 unconfirmed, not mapped."
  ],
